## 2. What I changed (and what I did not touch)

**New `memory_manager.py`** (no Gradio inside, so it is easy to test): database, login, classification, decision, save, read, delete, prompt building.

**`app.py` changes (only these):**
1. `import` of `memory_manager` + memory settings + database start-up (top of file).
2. `MAX_HISTORY_MESSAGES` now comes from `SHORT_TERM_MEMORY_LIMIT` (env var, default 10) and has a slider.
3. `assemble_prompt(...)` got 3 new optional arguments (`memory_text`, `memory_items`, `history_limit`). The memory block is added to the system prompt after the student profile.
4. `send_message(...)` runs the memory steps before calling Groq, and returns 6 extra outputs (consent box, trace, saved list).
5. `preview_prompt(...)` only *reads* memories. It never saves anything and costs no API call.
6. New section **10B** (login, consent, view, delete functions) and a new **🧬 Memory** tab + consent box in the UI.
7. A short Memory paragraph in the Concepts tab.

Everything else (RAG, grounding, trusted sources, classification tab, evaluation, verification, experiments, formats, constraints, quick prompts) is untouched.

