## 3. Complete data flow (step by step)

```
Student types a message
   │
   1. WHO is this?        mem_user (state) → user_id   (not logged in → no long-term memory)
   2. CLASSIFY            classify_memory_all()  → LONG_TERM / SHORT_TERM / NO_PERMANENT  (JSON, validated)
   3. DECIDE              decide_memory_action() → ASK_CONSENT / SKIP_UNCERTAIN / KEEP_SHORT_TERM / DO_NOT_SAVE ...
   4. RETRIEVE            get_memory_context()   → saved memories of THIS user only → text block
   5. BUILD PROMPT        assemble_prompt()      → rules + profile + memory block + course/RAG data + last N messages
   6. ASK GROQ            llm_call()             → answer shown in chat
   7. CONSENT BOX         if something worth saving was found → "Save to memory?" [Save] [Don't save]
   8. SAVE (only on Save) approve_pending() → save_memory() → PostgreSQL (UPSERT, no duplicates)
```

**Tanglish:** Student message anuppina → (1) yaar user nu paarkum → (2) message-a classify pannum → (3) save pannalama nu mudivu edukkum → (4) database-la irundhu andha user oda memory mattum edukkum → (5) prompt build pannum → (6) Groq-ku anuppi answer edukkum → (7) save panna kaetkum (consent) → (8) "Save" click panna mattum database-la save aagum.

**Short-term vs long-term**

| | Short-term | Long-term |
|---|---|---|
| Where | Chat window (Gradio) | PostgreSQL table `user_memory` |
| How long | Current session | Until you delete it |
| What | Recent questions and answers | Name, level, language, interests, goal |
| Saved when | Automatically (chat history) | Only after your **consent** |

